<title>BELGIUM: Belgian municipalities to sell more Dexia shares.</title>
<headline>Belgian municipalities to sell more Dexia shares.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Holding Communal, a holding company 100 percent owned by Belgium's municipalities, said in a statement on Wednesday it had decided to sell up to 15.5 percent more of its Dexia Belgium shares in the market through a global offering scheduled for the second quarter of 1997, probably June.</p>
<p>Dexia Belgium, 65.5 percent owned by Holding Communal, owns 50 percent of Belgian bank Credit Communal/Gemeentekrediet (CCB) and 50 percent of French Credit Local de France.</p>
</text>
